  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to mudslide in Corinto, Cauca Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ACIN (Asociaci&#xf3;n de Cabildos Ind&#xed;genas del Norte del Cauca), the is the coordinating body for the Cabildos or authorities of 18 indigenous reserves/resguardos in Northern Cauca, Colombia. They are responding to mudslides which happened in November 2017 in Corinto. In the rural areas of the Paez Peoples territory in Corinto municipality the ACIN Health Programme is supporting the rebuilding of housing lost in the mud slide. The project will contribute with materials for the rebuilding in accordance with Indigenous practices and beliefs, while the community will be providing the workforce and logistic support. This project is going to directly support 60 Indigenous families in the rural area of Corinto (corrugated roof sheets for 60 families and sanitary facilities for 20 out of the 60 families).</narrative>
  </description>
